                <pb facs="0821" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/3208: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-19T11:00:00+01:00">September 19, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 19—8:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. At meeting Diplomatic Corps Friday evening unanimously decided to ignore
                    suggestion concerning Madrid. British, French, Argentine and other nationals
                    with Embassies open there with Chargé <pb facs="0822" n="723" xml:id="pg723"/>
                    d’ Affaires took position suggestion could not apply to them. Am still convinced
                    it was aimed at Italy, Germany and Portugal, who have closed Embassies in Madrid
                    and moved to Alicante.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
